A||||2||PaulVoorduin||Disconnect el. connnector on Firewall ?||||5||
Z||000000||PaulVoorduin||10-18-2001||07:51 AM||||Hello,<P>I have a Fiero V6 GT '87 and I have a mouting question.<BR>How do you disconnect the electrical connector on the firewall joist under the rear window,<BR>in which all wires come together that goes to your engine.<BR>Thank you for your help.<BR> <BR>Greetings<BR> <BR>Paul||||reg||5
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||10-18-2001||07:58 AM||||It is held on with a plastic clip. Slide clip toward passenger side and remove. Then depress the holding force clip by depressing it's button and shove it through to the engine compartment.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rodrv6||10-18-2001||09:19 AM||||Just to clarify, it's not a connector, but a fancy grommet in the firewall.  After you remove the rear console you'll see where the harness unplugs at the ECM and just below it.  Feed it through like Indiana Resto Guy says.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  <BR>White 88 GT :)||||reg||1
